option "operating_currency" "USD"

; The second, worse consequence in the PLAN.md §5.2 defect note: an overspent
; envelope did not merely inflate `available`, it *silenced* the
; over-allocation guard. This ledger is genuinely over-allocated and the old
; formula reported it as fine.
;
;   cash            = 200 - 100 = 100
;   Groceries       = 50 - 100  = -50   (overspent by 50)
;   Dining Out      = 150 - 0   = 150   (untouched, fully committed)
;   Sigma balances  = 100
;   Sigma max(b, 0) = 150
;   available       = 100 - 150 = -50   -> over-allocated, verify MUST fail
;
; Old formula: `cash - Sigma balances` = 100 - 100 = 0, which passes
; `available >= 0` and reports verify: OK. But 150 is still committed to
; Dining Out and only 100 remains in the bank, so that money does not exist.
;
; Note why the old form could never catch this: `cash - Sigma balances`
; algebraically reduces to `inflows - Sigma allocations`, so spending
; cancelled out of it entirely and it could only ever detect allocating more
; than has ever come in.

2026-01-01 open Equity:Opening-Balances
2026-01-01 open Assets:Checking            USD
2026-01-01 open Expenses:Food:Groceries    USD
2026-01-01 open Expenses:Food:Dining       USD

2026-01-01 custom "envelope" "map" "Expenses:Food:Groceries" "Groceries"
2026-01-01 custom "envelope" "map" "Expenses:Food:Dining"    "Dining Out"

2026-01-01 custom "envelope" "allocate" "Groceries"   50.00 USD
2026-01-01 custom "envelope" "allocate" "Dining Out" 150.00 USD

2026-01-01 * "Opening balance"
    Assets:Checking      200.00 USD
    Equity:Opening-Balances

2026-01-05 * "Groceries"
    Assets:Checking      -100.00 USD
    Expenses:Food:Groceries
